# Platform-specific settings, imported by `.bazelrc` last. This tracked file is
# intentionally empty: it exists so the import always resolves, and it is where a
# genuinely shared platform fact lands when one appears — a runner toolchain, a
# platform-only flag — because its content belongs to the repository, not to a
# developer. A per-developer override goes to a user rc instead (user.bazelrc and
# the variants), which is ignored by git; never put secrets in either.
# `build:clang` / `build:gcc16` in `.bazelrc` are the shared entry points.
